  "chapterFindings": [
    "Arnold combines verses 1.26 and 1.27 into a single unified sentence describing relatives across both armies, accurately represented as a shared source span.",
    "Verse 1.43 is a genuine source omission flagged by Arnold in footnote 1 (\"Some repetitionary lines are here omitted\"), and 1.44 preserves only the closing clause \"So teach our holy hymns\" (ityanu\u015bu\u015bruma).",
    "Arnold translation in 1.10 renders apary\u0101ptam as \"Weakest\" and pary\u0101ptam as \"something too strong\", reflecting his poetic translation choice rather than an alignment fault."
